WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.790
Badwater Basin, Death Valley,
in California's Mojave Desert.

2
00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:08.450
Badwater lies 86 metres below sea level.

3
00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:14.430
Above it rises Telescope
Peak, 3,368 metres high.

4
00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:18.990
Salt flats cover about 520
square kilometres of the floor.

5
00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:21.850
Rain averages about 50 millimetres a year:

6
00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:23.410
about two inches.

7
00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:28.530
So what built a landscape this deep,
in a place that gets almost no rain?

8
00:00:28.580 --> 00:00:32.210
In this mission, you'll find out
what makes Death Valley so dry,

9
00:00:32.260 --> 00:00:33.950
and so deep.

10
00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:37.850
Then you'll follow a chain of landforms
from mountain front to salt pan,

11
00:00:37.900 --> 00:00:40.870
and see how quickly each one changes.

12
00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:44.210
Your mission: explain what
built Death Valley's landscape,

13
00:00:44.260 --> 00:00:46.680
in a place with almost no rain.
